---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const testCommands = `sudo pacman -S --needed rust bun webkit2gtk-4.1 base-devel curl wget file openssl appmenu-gtk-module libappindicator-gtk3 librsvg xdotool
cd "$HOME/Linux-Defender"
git switch revival/unified-app
cargo test --workspace --locked
cd desktop
bun install --frozen-lockfile
bun run tauri dev`;
---

<section id="install" class="container-tight py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <span class="eyebrow">Test the development build</span>
    <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Build Linux Defender on CachyOS</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 lede">
      Linux Defender 0.6.0 is still a source build. Signed installers and a one-click package are not published yet. The command below installs the Arch/Tauri build tools, runs the workspace tests, and starts the desktop app from the existing checkout.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border hairline bg-white/[0.02]">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b hairline px-5 py-4 sm:px-7">
      <div>
        <p class="font-semibold text-white">CachyOS / Arch Linux</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-white/50">Rust, Bun, GTK 3, WebKitGTK 4.1, and build tools</p>
      </div>
      <a class="text-sm text-clam-sage hover:text-white" href="https://v2.tauri.app/start/prerequisites/" rel="noopener">Tauri prerequisites</a>
    </div>
    <div class="relative p-5 sm:p-7">
      <pre class="term term-body !m-0 whitespace-pre overflow-x-auto text-[13px] leading-relaxed"><code>{testCommands}</code></pre>
      <button type="button" data-copy data-copy-text={testCommands} class="absolute right-8 top-8 rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-black/40 px-2.5 py-1.5 text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-white/70 transition hover:bg-black/60 hover:text-white">Copy</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Local engine and definitions</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/65">Install host ClamAV and let the system's FreshClam service or timer update its shared database. Linux Defender does not bundle ClamAV or create a second signature database.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Current testing boundary</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/65">The development build uses transitional Linux Defender package and data identifiers. Back up app data before testing; legacy settings migration and the signed release packages are still being completed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
    <a href={`${base}/docs/installation/`} class="text-clam-sage hover:text-white">Installation status</a>
    <a href={`${base}/docs/contributing/development/`} class="text-clam-sage hover:text-white">Build guide</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/Linux-Defender/Linux-Defender/releases" rel="noopener" class="text-clam-sage hover:text-white">Linux Defender releases</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/Linux-Defender/Linux-Defender/issues" rel="noopener" class="text-clam-sage hover:text-white">Report a bug</a>
  </div>
</section>
